#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:48
#, php-format
msgid "When you vote while you are logged in, we store your vote with your account. When you vote without an account, we store a cookie named %s in your browser for one year, so that the site remembers your votes. The cookie holds a random number and nothing else about you."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: name of a cookie.
#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:53
#, php-format
msgid "Where a board asks you to confirm your email address to vote or suggest a feature without an account, we store that address, and the name you give when you suggest one. We email you a link to confirm it. Once you do, we store a cookie named %s in your browser for one year, so that the site knows it is you. The cookie holds a number and a signature, nothing else about you. We then email you when the status of a request you voted for or suggested changes. Every email has a link that stops these emails."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:56
msgid "When you are logged in and you vote for a request, suggest one or press its Follow button, we store that you follow that request, and we email you when its status changes. Every email has a link that stops these emails, and you can also stop them in your profile."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:57
msgid "To limit how often one visitor can vote or send requests, we count attempts per IP address for up to one hour. The count is stored under a scrambled form of the address that cannot be turned back into it. We do not store your IP address."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: URL of Akismet's privacy policy.
#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:63
#, php-format
msgid "New feature requests are checked by Akismet, an anti-spam service. It receives the text of the request, the name and email address you gave, your IP address and the name of your browser. Akismet has its own <a href=\"%s\">privacy policy</a>."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: URL of Cloudflare's privacy policy for Turnstile.
#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:71
#, php-format
msgid "The form for suggesting a feature is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, which checks that a person, not a program, sends it. While the form is open, Cloudflare receives your IP address and details of your browser and device. Cloudflare has its own <a href=\"%s\">privacy policy for Turnstile</a>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:76
msgid "This plugin stores feature requests, votes, and which requests a user follows, in your site's database. The text below describes that. Leave out what your site does not use, such as the sentence about voting without an account when none of your boards allow it."
